{
  "requirement": "The agent accounts for each delivered `search_structure` result under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.search.finish_search.inputs`, including an empty\nresult. A separate tracked read of a matched item records its own dependency.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.search.search_structure.inputs`. The requirement has two obligations.\n\n**Obligation 1: each delivered `search_structure` result is accounted for under `finish_search.inputs`, including an empty result.**\n- `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot` runs an empty `search_structure` on a peer session.\n  - It asserts `matches` is `[]` and the first-search instructions are present.\n  - It asserts `outstanding_searches()` lists exactly that `search_id`.\n  - It asserts `finish_search` with `used:[]` succeeds and yields no dependencies.\n- The same test covers the wider `finish_search` contract, through `search_text` and paging:\n  - Selecting a tag twice yields the same original-snapshot dependency.\n  - Earlier selections survive later calls.\n  - An invalid `finish_search` call is rejected.\n  - After the rejected call, `outstanding_searches().len()` is still 2.\n  - Another session cannot close the search.\n- `empty_structural_search_results_remain_discovery` (in `agent/tests.rs`) asserts that an empty structural result is `{\"complete\":true,\"matches\":[]}`. It also asserts there are no dependencies and no observation callback.\n- `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` and `fixed_tools_deliver_domain_contents_with_mandatory_snapshot_dependencies` assert that a `search_structure` delivery has empty dependencies and does not read domain content.\n- `structural_tags_select_only_the_original_enclosing_item` finishes a structural search with `used:[]`, which adds no dependency.\n  - It then selects the tag for `fn[two]` after the file has changed on disk.\n  - The recorded `Dependency::Node(\"code.rs#fn[two]\", fingerprint)` matches the original snapshot's fingerprint.\n  - Selecting the tag again preserves that dependency.\n  - Unselected matches add no dependency.\n- `search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging` runs `search_structure` and `search_text` through the same loop. It selects the tag and asserts the dependency is the enclosing `fn[chosen]` node at the snapshot fingerprint.\n- Paging and open-search tracking are shared across both search tools (`pages.rs#impl[Pages<N, L>]/fn[search]`, `outstanding`), so the `search_text` paging checks apply to structural results too. I checked this only from search snippets, not by reading the paging code.\n\n**Obligation 2: a separate tracked read of a matched item records its own dependency.**\n- `cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input` runs `search_structure`, then `outline_source`, then `read_source` of `fn[observed]`, then a failing read.\n  - The final dependency list is exactly one `Dependency::Node` with the selected-content fingerprint.\n  - The search itself and the failed read add no dependency.\n- `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` asserts the observation callback runs only for reads (selectors `\"\"`, `\"\"` and `fn[chosen]`), not for search pages.\n- `fixed_tools_deliver_domain_contents_with_mandatory_snapshot_dependencies` asserts `read_source` records the dependency from the prepared domain content.\n\nI found no plausible violating behavior that these tests would accept, so I report no gaps.",
  "references": "6ded9434dcc35ca3111675a3dca576dac7db64c0ade7a7f10698f0fe970422eb",
